# Data Model

## IndexedDB stores

Two object stores, both keyed by `id` (UUID string):

| Store | Key type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `packLists` | `string` | Predefined reusable pack lists |
| `packings` | `string` | Active or completed packing sessions |

## PackList

```ts
type PackList = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  items: readonly string[];          // ordered list of item text strings
  referencedListIds: readonly string[]; // IDs of other PackLists included by this list
  createdAt: string;                 // ISO 8601
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

### Constraints

- No circular references: before saving, validate the full dependency graph.
- A PackList may only be deleted if no other PackList references it.

## Packing

```ts
type PackingItemStatus = 'pending' | 'packed' | 'discarded';

type PackingItem = {
  listId: string;   // source PackList id
  text: string;
  status: PackingItemStatus;
};

type PackingStatus = 'active' | 'done';

type Packing = {
  id: string;
  name: string;
  date: string;                      // ISO 8601 date (YYYY-MM-DD)
  packListIds: readonly string[];    // selected root pack-lists
  items: readonly PackingItem[];     // expanded and frozen at creation
  status: PackingStatus;
  createdAt: string;
  updatedAt: string;
}
```

### Item expansion

When a Packing is created, `packListIds` is resolved recursively:
- Only **leaf lists** (lists with no `referencedListIds`) contribute items.
- Items are grouped by their source `listId` for display.
- The expanded item list is frozen into `items` at creation time (snapshot semantics — later edits to a PackList do not affect an existing Packing).

### Status transitions

- `active` → `done` automatically when all items are `packed` or `discarded`.
- A Packing is discarded by deletion, not by a status field.

## DB layer

All DB access goes through `src/db/`. Never call `idb` directly from a screen or component.
Functions follow verb-first naming: `getPackList`, `savePackList`, `deletePackList`, `getAllPackings`, etc.
